Live MIDI survives the graph rebuild a MIDI note edit triggers

Every MIDI note add/remove rebuilds the playback graph (tracktion_Edit.cpp
childAddedOrRemoved restarts on IDs::NOTE). LiveMidiInjectingNode carries
its pending injected messages across such rebuilds by finding its old
counterpart via nodeID -- but that id hashes the node's whole input chain,
and LoopingMidiNode hashes its sequences into its own id, so a note edit
changes the very id the lookup needs. The migration misses on exactly the
rebuild every note edit causes, and any not-yet-processed live MIDI is
stranded in the outgoing graph.

In an app that previews notes as they are drawn (playGuideNote on the
same mouse-down that writes the note), the note-on usually sits pending
when the rebuild lands a few milliseconds later, so previews were lost
depending on audio-callback timing -- observed failing roughly 2 times in
3, and reliably on the first edit after launch.

Fixed by falling back to matching the old node by track, of which each
graph holds at most one. Renders are unaffected: they build one graph
with no predecessor, so the fallback never runs.

diff --git a/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_LiveMidiInjectingNode.cpp b/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_LiveMidiInjectingNode.cpp
index eaedaa5..1ea6b58 100644
--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_LiveMidiInjectingNode.cpp
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_LiveMidiInjectingNode.cpp
@@ -45,15 +45,33 @@ std::vector<tracktion::graph::Node*> LiveMidiInjectingNode::getDirectInputNodes(
 
 void LiveMidiInjectingNode::prepareToPlay (const tracktion::graph::PlaybackInitialisationInfo& info)
 {
+    auto transferFrom = [this] (LiveMidiInjectingNode& oldNode)
+    {
+        const juce::ScopedLock sl2 (oldNode.liveMidiLock);
+        liveMidiMessages.swapWith (oldNode.liveMidiMessages);
+        midiSourceID = oldNode.midiSourceID;
+    };
+
     if (auto oldNode = findNodeWithIDIfNonZero<LiveMidiInjectingNode> (info.nodeGraphToReplace, getNodeProperties().nodeID))
     {
         if (oldNode->track == track)
         {
-            const juce::ScopedLock sl2 (oldNode->liveMidiLock);
-            liveMidiMessages.swapWith (oldNode->liveMidiMessages);
-            midiSourceID = oldNode->midiSourceID;
+            transferFrom (*oldNode);
+            return;
         }
     }
+
+    // The nodeID above hashes this node's whole input chain, and any MIDI
+    // note edit changes that hash (LoopingMidiNode hashes its sequences into
+    // its id) -- so the lookup misses on exactly the graph rebuild every note
+    // edit triggers, stranding pending live MIDI (e.g. note previews) in the
+    // outgoing graph. Fall back to matching by track, of which each graph
+    // holds at most one of these nodes. (carve)
+    if (info.nodeGraphToReplace != nullptr)
+        for (auto n : info.nodeGraphToReplace->orderedNodes)
+            if (auto oldNode = dynamic_cast<LiveMidiInjectingNode*> (n))
+                if (oldNode->track == track)
+                    return transferFrom (*oldNode);
 }
 
 bool LiveMidiInjectingNode::isReadyToProcess()
